<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Tuesday, barrows and gilts were $1.00 higher. $52.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>Interior Iowa moved 100,000 hogs Tuesday. Severely cold weather continued to reduced marketings, adding some strength to live cash prices.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	230-270 lbs    52.00-52.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3	270-280 lbs    52.00</p>
<p>    US 1-2 package  213 lbs    50.50</p>
<p>Sows - steady/off $3.00. Top $53.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2    300-500 lbs    43.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3    500-550 lbs    50.00</p>
<p>		  550-700 lbs    52.00-53.00</p>
<p>    Boars:    300-700 lbs    40.00</p>
<p>		  200-300 lbs    41.00</p>
</text>
